{{HeartsTableRowDesc|1 = A Wizard's Garden|2 = The Farmer comes across Magnus working at his Ancient Fruit crops. He is adding a magical pesticide to keep insects away. He says that in addition to keeping away bugs, he has to protect them with magic from his ex-wife's hexes. Magnus shares that while he likes his role in the valley, it has been difficult having his heart broken twice. If he ever loves again though, it would likely be for someone who appreciates plants, prompting the Farmer to say:
* '''"My farm has an awful lot of plants...""'''
Magnus laughs and reminds the Farmer that beyond plants, there is still the cauldron smell to get used to. He then heads inside, saying he has some business to attend to and asking the Farmer to stop by again soon.
* '''"That shouldn't be too hard to find around here."'''
Magnus reflects on the number of people in the valley with talents for plant growing and ponders that it might come from living so close to nature. He then heads inside, saying he has some business to attend to and asking the Farmer to stop by again soon.}}
{{TableEnd}}</div></div>

===Hearts: 8===
<div class="mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" data-expandtext="❇ Show ❇" data-collapsetext="✖ Hide ✖">{{Hearts|8}} <div class=mw-collapsible-toggle-placeholder></div>
