{{HeartsTableRowDesc|1 = Junimo Rising|2 = The Farmer enter's the Wizard's Tower to find Magnus on his summoning circle surrounded by excited Junimos. He attempted to cast a spell to communicate with them more, and it backfires causing the Junimos to have an increased interest in him. He asks the Farmer to read some lines of a spell in his magic book to help with the rambunctious Junimos. All but one of the Junimos disappear after the spell is read, and Magnus asks them where they come from in the forest. The screen fades and a message displays, describing their time with the Junimo and the forest spirit's eventual departure. Afterward, Magnus asks the Farmer whether they were suppressing a laugh over Magnus being jumped on by the Junimos. They respond either:
* '''"Never, crossed my mind."'''
Magnus doesn't quite believe the Farmer, but appreciates they are trying to spare his feelings. He suggests next time he might visit the Junimos in the forest, rather than try to summon them again. Before going to explore the woods, he asks the Farmer to keep the story to themselves.
* '''"To be honest... yes, absolutely."'''
Magnus laughs and suggests next time he might visit the Junimos in the forest, rather than try to summon them again. Before going to explore the woods, he asks the Farmer to keep the story to themselves.}}
{{TableEnd}}</div></div>

